Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: an agent with no radio ready does not hold every policy

The lab's 0187 sends an explicit set_policy from one radio of the agent that is ready for it,
and when none is, it took the agent's first radio anyway. A command on a radio that is not
ready waits out its time limit and is cancelled, and the next set_policy for the agent is pushed
on it again; set_policy commands run one at a time, so every agent's policy waits behind it. On
rdk-1004 (9 October, gateway image 21) a Wi-Fi extender sent no M1 after the controller's
restart: its set_policy was pushed 23 times and cancelled on its time limit 7 times in 13
minutes, no Policy Config Request went to it, and the lab runtime's metrics policy (POST
metricsreporting/enable) never succeeded, three cold starts in a row.

Now the command goes to a radio in a state for a policy, idle if one is, else busy with
another command (it waits for that, as before). An agent with no radio in such a state gets no
command: its policy goes to the live model and the database at once, as a completed command
commits it (commit_set_policy, shared with the command's completion), the command completes,
and the agent gets that policy in its onboarding's own policy step, from the live model, and
its metric reporting part at each topology sync. Another agent's policy is no longer held by
it.

Platform-independent (completes the lab's 0187); not for upstream on its own.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [completes 0187, a lab patch]

diff --git a/inc/em_orch_ctrl.h b/inc/em_orch_ctrl.h
index cc38ec5..a4e9971 100644
--- a/inc/em_orch_ctrl.h
+++ b/inc/em_orch_ctrl.h
@@ -94,7 +94,18 @@ public:
 	 * @returns True if the EM is ready for orchestration finalization, false otherwise.
 	 */
 	bool is_em_ready_for_orch_fini(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em);
-    
+
+	/**!
+	 * @brief Commits a set_policy command's policies to the agent's live data model and the DB.
+	 *
+	 * Done when the command completes on its radio, or at once for an agent with no radio
+	 * ready for a policy, which gets the committed policy in its onboarding's policy step.
+	 *
+	 * @param[in] pcmd The set_policy command.
+	 * @param[in] em A radio of the agent the command is for.
+	 */
+	void commit_set_policy(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em);
+
 	/**!
 	 * @brief Handles the orchestration of transient commands.
 	 *
